WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.508 --> 00:00:10.969
Well. at the very least. we can
thank god it was a parked car you hit.

2
00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.491
What about the dui? Is there
any way to get that thrown out?

3
00:00:14.515 --> 00:00:17.476
I don't know who the judge is yet.
but most of them won't throw out a dui.

4
00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:21.998
Our best bet. since it's a first offense.
is to plead it down to a misdemeanor.

5
00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:25.376
Suspended license. alcohol
education classes. community service.

6
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.004
And is there any way we can
get it cleared from her record?

7
00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:30.072
I will try to get the record sealed.

8
00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:34.344
Honestly. it would be easier if she
was headed to college in the fall.

9
00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:36.745
Is her declining
Princeton already official?

10
00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:40.099
- Afraid so.
- Shit.

11
00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:41.601
Jesus Christ.

12
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:43.043
I'm sorry. what?

13
00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:45.587
- Nothing.
- Good.

14
00:00:46.547 --> 00:00:49.234
Look. Tori's a good kid who's
never been in any trouble.

15
00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:51.653
I will try to push that as far as I can.

16
00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:53.530
That's it? There's
nothing else we can do?

17
00:00:53.554 --> 00:00:56.491
Her pretrial conference
is Wednesday at 3:00 P.M.

18
00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:58.725
Usually. we can work it all out right there.

19
00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.145
This is gonna be okay.
you guys. I promise.

20
00:01:02.813 --> 00:01:05.792
But it's not going to disappear
with a wink and a handshake.

21
00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:07.669
and I think we all need to accept that.

22
00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:08.753
This is crazy.

23
00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:11.047
I was just moving my car
so someone could get out.

24
00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.299
- You think that's the crazy part here?
- Mel.

25
00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:17.119
No. she is not taking any
responsibility for her actions here.

26
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.496
What about your actions?

27
00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.707
We're not talking about me.

28
00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:25.335
Were you sober when you decided
to throw shit at your neighbors?

29
00:01:25.878 --> 00:01:27.480
- Hey.
- She's such a hypocrite.

30
00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:28.648
No. she isn't.

31
00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:30.942
She's your mother. and
she's worried about you. okay?

32
00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:32.652
Whatever issues you
happen to have with us.

33
00:01:32.676 --> 00:01:35.321
you waived your right to complain
about them when you did what you did.

34
00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.073
I'm sorry if you don't think it's fair.

35
00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.391
but right now. honestly. I
don't give a shit about fair.

36
00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:42.495
What I give a shit
about is looking after you.

37
00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:45.606
since you clearly can't be
bothered to do it yourself.

38
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:47.208
Now. go wait outside.

39
00:01:47.232 --> 00:01:49.818
I'll be out in a few minutes
to take you to school.

40
00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:58.911
I don't want you at my hearing.

41
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

42
00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:10.523
- Sorry about her.
- No. don't. Don't apologize.

43
00:02:10.547 --> 00:02:12.841
I'm gonna get you
through this. I promise.

44
00:02:14.218 --> 00:02:17.513
But I do think maybe you should
let Coop handle the hearing.

45
00:02:18.305 --> 00:02:19.282
I'm her mother.

46
00:02:19.306 --> 00:02:21.284
Mel. it's a small court.

47
00:02:21.308 --> 00:02:23.495
and we can assume word of
your arrest has gotten around.

48
00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:25.437
I just don't want to muddy the waters.

49
00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.148
Speaking of which.

50
00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:32.712
I am pushing to keep your
issues out of the court entirely.

51
00:02:32.736 --> 00:02:33.796
- Okay.
- You can do that?

52
00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:37.342
If you offer your neighbor a sincere
apology and take care of the cleanup.

53
00:02:37.366 --> 00:02:39.135
there's a chance this will just go away.

54
00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.327
Wink and a handshake.

55
00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:43.747
You want me to apologize to
those assholes? Absolutely not.

56
00:02:44.248 --> 00:02:47.101
Are you fucking kidding me right
now? She's handing you a massive win.

57
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:49.805
- It's the principle of the thing.
- Now you care about principles?

58
00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.130
Apologize and be done with it.

59
00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:56.093
Kat. they let their dog run wild.
Surely there are laws against that.

60
00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:59.155
It's irresponsible and dangerous.
He could get hit by a truck.

61
00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:01.324
If you don't do it. this
could become a felony.

62
00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:02.432
- What?
- What?

63
00:03:03.642 --> 00:03:05.995
I thought the charge
would be criminal mischief.

64
00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.957
It bumps up to a class d felony
if the damages exceed $1.500.

65
00:03:08.981 --> 00:03:11.125
Which is less than one
landscaping bill for these people.

66
00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:15.237
Plus. they have you on camera delivering
a bag of excrement to their door.

67
00:03:16.238 --> 00:03:17.799
I'm sorry. what's this now?

68
00:03:17.823 --> 00:03:19.342
It was dog shit.

69
00:03:19.366 --> 00:03:22.887
So. they have the bones of an intentional
infliction of emotional distress case

70
00:03:22.911 --> 00:03:24.973
if they want to tie you
up in civil court as well.

71
00:03:24.997 --> 00:03:26.641
My god. You cannot be serious.

72
00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:28.434
Emotional distress?
What about my distress?

73
00:03:28.458 --> 00:03:30.502
Kat. can you just... Can
you give us a minute?

74
00:03:31.253 --> 00:03:32.713
Yeah. I'll go check on Tori.

75
00:03:36.341 --> 00:03:37.342
This is insane.

76
00:03:38.677 --> 00:03:40.780
Okay. what the fuck is
going on with you right now?

77
00:03:40.804 --> 00:03:43.116
- Nothing.
- You brought them a bag of shit?

78
00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.618
- It was their dog. I was making a point.
- Come on.

79
00:03:45.642 --> 00:03:47.871
Normal people don't behave that way.

80
00:03:47.895 --> 00:03:50.623
- That's not normal behavior. Mel.
- I asked these people

81
00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:52.834
50 million times to curb their dog.

82
00:03:52.858 --> 00:03:54.502
"Keep your dog in your own yard."

83
00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:56.379
They ignored me time and again.

84
00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:59.656
They never took me seriously.

85
00:04:00.449 --> 00:04:02.284
They made me feel like I was nothing.

86
00:04:05.204 --> 00:04:06.205
How do you feel now?

87
00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:14.630
Exactly. You have to apologize to them.

88
00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:20.385
I have to take our daughter to school.

89
00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:26.558
For the record...

90
00:04:29.186 --> 00:04:31.104
I'm officially worried about you.

91
00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.838
The coopers are really becoming
a cottage industry for me.

92
00:04:56.964 --> 00:04:57.941
Well. what can I say?

93
00:04:57.965 --> 00:05:00.175
Mel was impressed with
how you handled my case.

94
00:05:00.759 --> 00:05:03.822
Yeah. Well. these two fall
under a different category.

95
00:05:03.846 --> 00:05:04.930
And what's that?

96
00:05:05.514 --> 00:05:08.225
Mel's a close friend. so I
won't be sending her a bill.

97
00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:09.911
That's very nice of you.

98
00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:12.896
I'll be sending it to you.
and my rates just went up.

99
00:05:13.939 --> 00:05:14.940
Fair enough.

100
00:05:24.199 --> 00:05:27.870
<i>I could still remember every
detail about the day Tori was born.</i>

101
00:05:28.453 --> 00:05:30.515
<i>How impossibly light she felt in my arms.</i>

102
00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:32.475
<i>How she sounded when she cried.</i>

103
00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:33.935
<i>How she smelled.</i>

104
00:05:33.959 --> 00:05:35.687
<i>How she waved her tiny fingers</i>

105
00:05:35.711 --> 00:05:38.297
<i>like she was conducting an
orchestra only she could hear.</i>

106
00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.552
<i>I made a lot of promises
that day to her and to myself.</i>

107
00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:47.699
<i>And over the years. I'd kept most
and undoubtedly broken a few.</i>

108
00:05:47.723 --> 00:05:51.185
<i>but nothing prepared me for the
shock of seeing my little girl behind bars.</i>

109
00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:56.374
<i>And the problem was I couldn't credibly
talk to my daughter about her bad choices</i>

110
00:05:56.398 --> 00:06:00.027
<i>when I seemed to be making more
and more of them with each passing day.</i>

111
00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:04.007
<i>If I was gonna be any
kind of parent to her.</i>

112
00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:06.742
<i>I was gonna have to
start righting my own ship.</i>

113
00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.944
- Hi.
- Hi.

114
00:06:42.444 --> 00:06:44.029
Thanks for seeing me.

115
00:06:44.613 --> 00:06:46.031
In-person visit.

116
00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:48.909
I have to admit. I'm intrigued.

117
00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:51.954
And by intrigued. I mean concerned.

118
00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:55.249
- I haven't been here since...
- Yeah.

119
00:06:57.668 --> 00:06:59.670
- Drink?
- No. thank you. I won't be staying.

120
00:07:00.254 --> 00:07:01.494
That's what you said last time.

121
00:07:03.757 --> 00:07:06.069
- Sorry. I wasn't trying to...
- It's all right.

122
00:07:06.093 --> 00:07:08.387
Although. they can't fire you now.

123
00:07:12.391 --> 00:07:13.576
I don't know what I'm saying. I'm sorry.

124
00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.360
I don't know why I'm so anxious all
of a sudden. Do you want a drink?

125
00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:18.456
I already asked you that.

126
00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.148
- Are you okay?
- Sure.

127
00:07:20.983 --> 00:07:24.003
I mean. you could have just called. but
you didn't. So. clearly something is up.

128
00:07:24.027 --> 00:07:25.713
And while I can't seem to stop talking.

129
00:07:25.737 --> 00:07:28.365
whatever it is you're here for
is drilling a hole in my brain.

130
00:07:29.241 --> 00:07:31.451
Is Tommy burns still working
at Bailey in compliance?

131
00:07:32.035 --> 00:07:34.556
Yes. Tommy's still at Bailey.

132
00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.182
Why are you asking
me about compliance?

133
00:07:36.206 --> 00:07:39.334
I want you to have him look
at my excelsior investment.

134
00:07:39.918 --> 00:07:41.813
He didn't have to. The
investment didn't reach

135
00:07:41.837 --> 00:07:42.939
- the kyc threshold.
- I know.

136
00:07:42.963 --> 00:07:44.858
So. there was no reason
for compliance to do a review.

137
00:07:44.882 --> 00:07:45.942
- Right.
- But now.

138
00:07:45.966 --> 00:07:47.443
after the money has been transferred

139
00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:50.155
and we've both signed about
ten pounds of documents.

140
00:07:50.179 --> 00:07:52.407
you're asking me to essentially
launch an investigation...

141
00:07:52.431 --> 00:07:54.534
- That's right.
- Into your own business.

142
00:07:54.558 --> 00:07:57.561
Are you sure you won't have
that drink? I'm having a drink.

143
00:07:58.061 --> 00:08:01.416
- The money is gonna come back bad.
- I think you should stop talking.

144
00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.961
It can be traced through a series
of international dummy corporations

145
00:08:04.985 --> 00:08:07.172
- to a man named Owen ashe.
- Wow. you're still talking.

146
00:08:07.196 --> 00:08:09.757
Why couldn't you have just tried to
get me into bed like a normal person?

147
00:08:09.781 --> 00:08:11.676
- Liv.
- I haven't had time for a date in months.

148
00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.386
Your chances would have
actually been excellent.

149
00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.721
Owen ashe is on the ofac list.

150
00:08:14.745 --> 00:08:16.222
Fuck. Coop!

151
00:08:16.246 --> 00:08:17.915
Stop talking!

152
00:08:23.212 --> 00:08:25.690
Is this about Jack?

153
00:08:25.714 --> 00:08:27.817
Are you trying to take him down?

154
00:08:27.841 --> 00:08:29.736
Because I have to tell
you that's a long way to go

155
00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:31.488
- for petty revenge.
- This has nothing to do with Jack.

156
00:08:31.512 --> 00:08:33.239
Or me? You're angry that
I didn't stand up for you

157
00:08:33.263 --> 00:08:35.283
- when Jack fired you.
- It has nothing to do with any of that.

158
00:08:35.307 --> 00:08:37.183
No? Then what the hell is this?

159
00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:39.863
I'm just trying to do the right thing here.

160
00:08:41.438 --> 00:08:42.414
It seems to me

161
00:08:42.438 --> 00:08:44.375
- that ship has sailed. Coop. hasn't it?
- Maybe.

162
00:08:44.399 --> 00:08:45.919
And now you've dragged
me into your mess.

163
00:08:45.943 --> 00:08:47.420
- Listen. I had no idea...
- Again.

164
00:08:47.444 --> 00:08:49.339
That Jack was gonna have
you running point on this.

165
00:08:49.363 --> 00:08:51.591
- Why not? Because I fucked you?
- Because you're 28 years old.

166
00:08:51.615 --> 00:08:52.717
- for Christ's sake.
- I'm 29.

167
00:08:52.741 --> 00:08:53.801
- What?
- Nothing.

168
00:08:53.825 --> 00:08:56.161
- Listen to me...
- I'm begging you to stop talking.

169
00:08:59.122 --> 00:09:01.059
- Who knows?
- What?

170
00:09:01.083 --> 00:09:03.043
The ofac list. Who knows?

171
00:09:03.752 --> 00:09:05.271
Well. you now.

172
00:09:05.295 --> 00:09:09.299
Me and. you know. the
United States government.

173
00:09:12.678 --> 00:09:15.156
- I'm not talking to Tommy in compliance.
- Liv.

174
00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:17.867
You wanna blow up your
life. do it with someone else.

175
00:09:17.891 --> 00:09:19.994
This flew under the radar.
like you knew it would.

176
00:09:20.018 --> 00:09:21.746
- and that's where it will stay.
- Come on. Liv.

177
00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:23.581
- Stop repeating my name.
- You can't do this.

178
00:09:23.605 --> 00:09:24.958
I didn't do this!

179
00:09:24.982 --> 00:09:26.918
You did! You did this.

180
00:09:26.942 --> 00:09:28.837
And you don't get to send me packing

181
00:09:28.861 --> 00:09:31.339
because you're having some
kind of crisis of conscience.

182
00:09:31.363 --> 00:09:34.342
This isn't mad off. It's
not theranos or enron.

183
00:09:34.366 --> 00:09:36.302
- No one is getting hurt.
- We don't know that.

184
00:09:36.326 --> 00:09:37.595
It is an arbitrary list

185
00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:40.348
from a government riddled with
adhd that has no fucks to give.

186
00:09:40.372 --> 00:09:43.184
Wake up. Coop. It's
the wild west out there.

187
00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:45.544
No one is looking. and no one cares.

188
00:09:47.462 --> 00:09:48.839
Listen to me. I used to be...

189
00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.651
Where you are now.

190
00:09:51.675 --> 00:09:54.075
- Yeah. I doubt that strongly.
- There's a math that you do.

191
00:09:54.678 --> 00:09:56.364
Calculus of compromise. right?

192
00:09:56.388 --> 00:09:58.700
What am I willing to do to
get where I wanna be. right?

193
00:09:58.724 --> 00:10:01.035
Now. of course. once I get
there. I'll stop doing the thing.

194
00:10:01.059 --> 00:10:03.496
I'll stop taking risks
because I'll be there. not here.

195
00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.207
The thing is. you're never ever there.

196
00:10:06.231 --> 00:10:07.733
There's no there.

197
00:10:09.151 --> 00:10:10.444
You're always just here.

198
00:10:11.528 --> 00:10:13.173
In the interest of
ending this conversation.

199
00:10:13.197 --> 00:10:15.282
I'm going to pretend
that made any sense.

200
00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.701
You found a way back. Coop.

201
00:10:18.285 --> 00:10:21.371
Against all odds. and
no one is getting hurt.

202
00:10:22.581 --> 00:10:26.293
But if you blow this up. you and
me. we're the ones who get hurt.

203
00:10:27.794 --> 00:10:30.148
I lose my job and my reputation.

204
00:10:30.172 --> 00:10:34.051
I end up serving fish and chips at
my uncle's pub back in cheltenham.

205
00:10:34.843 --> 00:10:35.928
And you.

206
00:10:36.512 --> 00:10:39.139
you're looking at ten years
minimum if this gets out.

207
00:10:39.681 --> 00:10:41.993
And even if you beat that. and you won't.

208
00:10:42.017 --> 00:10:44.144
Jack will destroy you and your family.

209
00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:48.458
You'll be in litigation you can't
afford for the next ten years.

210
00:10:48.482 --> 00:10:50.067
Why risk any of this?

211
00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:57.199
I don't care about whatever
his fucking name is. Owen ashe.

212
00:10:59.576 --> 00:11:00.577
I care about you.

213
00:11:02.412 --> 00:11:03.389
and I care about me.

214
00:11:03.413 --> 00:11:04.581
He's a bad guy. Liv.

215
00:11:07.209 --> 00:11:08.210
So. you manage him.

216
00:11:10.254 --> 00:11:13.090
And I'll manage you.

217
00:11:25.769 --> 00:11:31.125
<i>A paper shadow in a house of stone</i>

218
00:11:31.149 --> 00:11:36.256
<i>the wooden flag of a drifting dreamboat</i>

219
00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:40.468
<i>I never knew how far
the ride was gonna go</i>

220
00:11:40.492 --> 00:11:44.013
<i>till I looked back at the smoke</i>

221
00:11:44.037 --> 00:11:49.269
<i>you can't keep up with the joneses</i>

222
00:11:49.293 --> 00:11:54.190
<i>don't wanna run for the roses</i>

223
00:11:54.214 --> 00:12:02.214
<i>I got my pocket of posies
sometimes I wonder why.</i>

224
00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:09.789
<i>I just don't run with the joneses</i>

225
00:12:09.813 --> 00:12:14.919
<i>don't wanna smell the dying roses</i>

226
00:12:14.943 --> 00:12:20.008
<i>I got my pocket full of posies</i>

227
00:12:20.032 --> 00:12:25.078
<i>I don't keep up with the joneses.</i>

228
00:12:40.344 --> 00:12:43.698
They were about to put up the
drywall when they fired their designer.

229
00:12:43.722 --> 00:12:45.891
They hate the layout.

230
00:12:46.391 --> 00:12:49.037
So. you have carte blanche
to redesign everything.

231
00:12:49.061 --> 00:12:52.916
But the pool right here. it stays the same.

232
00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:55.668
That's where it gets
the most direct sunlight.

233
00:12:55.692 --> 00:12:56.836
This lot is amazing.

234
00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:57.921
- Yeah.
- I know.

235
00:12:57.945 --> 00:13:00.006
They were gonna
